            <ArticleTitle>A case of ulcerative colitis presenting as vasculitic purpura.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with ulcerative colitis presenting with vasculitic purpura is reported. Abnormal liver function and purpura responded to panproctocolectomy. Purpura preceded the diagnosis of ulcerative colitis by three years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
